{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["U15"],
      "pins": ["U15.1", "U15.2", "U15.14"],
      "nets": ["+3V3", "GND"],
      "observed": "PCA9685PW address-select pin A0 (U15 pin 1) is tied to the +3V3 net, while A1 (pin 2) and A2 to A5 (pins 3, 4, 5, 24) are on GND. With A0 high the PWM driver responds at 0x41, not 0x40.",
      "expected": "The specification lists the PCA9685PW at I2C address 0x40, which requires A0 to be strapped to GND like the other address pins.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U15\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"A0\") (pintype \"input\"))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(node (ref \"U15\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"A1\") (pintype \"input\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "PWM/servo driver | FCCPeripherals | NXP PCA9685PW (I2C 16-ch PWM), I2C addr 0x40"}
      ],
      "impact": "The FCC cannot address the servo PWM driver at its intended 0x40 address, so servo/PWM outputs would not be commanded and the driver would appear missing on the bus.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["NAVC2"],
      "pins": ["NAVC2.12", "NAVC2.18", "NAVC2.63"],
      "nets": ["Net-(NAVC2-VSS-Pad18)", "unconnected-(NAVC2-VSSA-Pad12)"],
      "observed": "On the NAVC MCU (STM32F405RGTx), VSS pins 18 and 63 form a net that contains only those two pins and is not tied to GND. VSSA (pin 12) is also unconnected. The FCC MCU's VSS and VSSA pins are both on GND.",
      "expected": "All VSS and VSSA pins of the MCU should return to the ground net.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"144\") (name \"Net-(NAVC2-VSS-Pad18)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"63\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"passive\")))"},
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"280\") (name \"unconnected-(NAVC2-VSSA-Pad12)\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"NAVC2\") (pin \"12\") (pinfunction \"VSSA\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"}
      ],
      "impact": "Two ground pins of the navigation MCU and its analogue ground are floating, so the NAVC has an incomplete ground return and unreliable ADC and logic reference behaviour.",
      "confidence": 0.3
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The PCA9685 address strap ties A0 to +3V3 while the specification requires address 0x40, which points to a deliberate or accidental deviation. The NAVC MCU's VSS and VSSA pins are also not returned to GND, which is a secondary concern."
}

